# Personal Data Analyst — environment variables (example)
#
# Copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in real values when they are
# needed. ".env" and ".env.*" files are ignored by Git (except this
# example), so real values are never committed.
#
# Without these values the app works fully offline and sync is switched
# off: all data stays in the browser (IndexedDB).
#
# Sync (Phase 3) needs the two values below. For development they point
# to the local Supabase test server ("npm run db:start"; the values are
# shown by "npm run db:status": API URL and the publishable key).
# Variables starting with VITE_ are included in the code sent to the
# browser, so only public values may use that prefix.
#
# NEVER put the Supabase service-role key here or anywhere in the
# frontend: it bypasses Row Level Security.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key
